#: data/io.github.k-nowicki.BetterScreenshot.metainfo.xml.in:11
msgid ""
"Better Screenshot is a fork of GNOME Screenshot that adds what multi-monitor "
"setups need: capturing one specific monitor rather than every screen "
"stitched together. Pick the monitor from a drop-down, and the choice is "
"remembered for next time, so a routine screenshot costs a single click."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.k-nowicki.BetterScreenshot.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid ""
"Screenshots can also cover the whole desktop, a single window, or a selected "
"rectangular area. Captures are saved straight to your pictures folder "
"without a confirmation dialog, and the countdown releases the keyboard and "
"pointer, so open menus stay open and end up in the picture."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.k-nowicki.BetterScreenshot.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid ""
"It works the same on Wayland and X11, and can be driven from a key binding "
"with --monitor, which accepts either a monitor number or a connector name "
"such as DP-5."
msgstr ""

